{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeSymmetricAlgebra","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeSymmetricAlgebra","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeRegularRep"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.MarkovTraceFamily.tr_eq_symTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.MarkovTraceFamily.tr_eq_symTrace","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeSymmetricAlgebra.lean#L158-L162","doc":"**Uniqueness**: every Markov trace with parameter `z = 0` is the symmetrising trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.eq_zero_of_symTrace_mul_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.eq_zero_of_symTrace_mul_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeSymmetricAlgebra.lean#L148-L156","doc":"**Nondegeneracy**: if `q·qi` is a unit and `τ(x y) = 0` for all `y`, then `x = 0`.  So\n`H_{m+1}(q)` is a symmetric algebra over `K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.symTrace_mul_stdElt_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.symTrace_mul_stdElt_inv","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeSymmetricAlgebra.lean#L136-L146","doc":"`τ(x T_{w⁻¹}) = (q·qi)^{ℓ(w)} · [coefficient of T_w in x]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.symTrace_mul_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeCoset.symTrace_mul_comm","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/734